{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NiuGkYwbtNf5oo9pSwJPK5","type":"tool_result","content":"# payout — 가맹 파트너 일일 정산 파일 배치\n\n카드 매입 추출(`txns-YYYYMM.tsv`)에서 파트너별·일자별 정산 내역을 잘라 정산 파일(PAY-IF-03 rev.2)을 만들고,\n파일 전송 벤더 CLI(`vendor/bin/xferq`, 벤더가 바이너리로 제공)로 파트너 수신함에 올린다.\n\n## 실행\n\n```\nbin/payout run 20261005                    # extract → build → ship\nbin/payout manifest 20261005               # 그날 전송 CLI에 넘긴 파일과 접수 번호\nbin/payout receipts P001 20261001 20261007 # 파트너가 실제로 내려받을 수 있는 일자별 건수·금액\nbin/payout partners                        # 활성 파트너\n```\n\n스케줄러는 매일 07:00에 전날 일자로 `bin/payout run`을 돌리고, exit 0이 아니면 당직에게 알린다.\n`XFERQ_HOME`(전송 CLI 스풀 디렉터리)은 스케줄러 환경에서 지정한다. 벤더 사용법은 `vendor/bin/xferq --help`.\n\n## 구성\n\n| 경로 | 내용 |\n|------|------|\n| `bin/payout` | 진입점. 서브커맨드 분기, 단계 순차 실행 |\n| `steps/NN-*.sh` | 단계 스크립트(번호 순). 각자 `_env.sh`로 lib·설정을 읽는다 |\n| `lib/` | 공용 함수 (추출, 분할, 파일 본문, 파일 이름, 전송, 매니페스트, 수신 확인 등) |\n| `conf/payout.conf` | 디렉터리·파일 규격 설정. `PAYOUT_*` 환경변수로 덮어쓴다 |\n| `conf/partners.conf` | 파트너 목록(상태 I는 정지 — 파일을 만들지 않음) |\n| `fixtures/` | 샘플 매입 추출(운영 데이터에서 금액·번호를 바꾼 것) |\n| `tests/` | `bash tests/run.sh` — 단위 테스트 + 샘플 주간 E2E |\n\n## 정산 파일 규격 메모 (PAY-IF-03 rev.2)\n\n- 파일명: `HBP_SETTLE_<파트너코드>_<YYYYMMDD>.csv` — 파트너와 합의한 접두. 파트너 쪽 적재기는 이 접두로 파일을 고른다.\n- 파트너 적재기는 파일당 명세(D) 최대 20행까지만 받는다. 넘는 날은 여러 파일로 나눠 보낸다(헤더의 `n/총수`).\n- 본문: `H`(헤더) / `D`(명세, 거래당 1행) / `T`(트레일러 — 명세 건수·순액 합계). 줄 끝은 CRLF.\n- 정산은 주말 포함 매일 나간다. 거래가 없는 날도 빈 파일(H·T만)을 보낸다.\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Runs the full test suite.\nexec bash \"$(dirname \"$0\")/tests/run.sh\"\n----\nbin:\npayout\n\nconf:\npartners.conf\npayout.conf\n\nfixtures:\ntxns-202610.tsv\n\nlib:\nchunk.sh\ncommon.sh\ncsvfile.sh\ndates.sh\nmanifest.sh\nmoney.sh\nnaming.sh\nreceipts.sh\ntxns.sh\nxfer.sh\n\nsteps:\n10-extract.sh\n20-build.sh\n30-ship.sh\n_env.sh\n\ntests:\nlib.sh\nrun.sh\ntest_chunk.sh\ntest_csvfile.sh\ntest_dates.sh\ntest_partner_delivery.sh\n\nvendor:\nbin\n\nvendor/bin:\nxferq\n----\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# payout — merchant settlement files for card-acquiring partners.\n#\n#   payout run DATE                  extract → build → ship\n#   payout manifest DATE             files handed to the transfer CLI that day\n#   payout receipts PARTNER FROM TO  what the partner can download, per day\n#   payout partners                  active partner codes\n#\n# DATE is YYYYMMDD. Configuration: conf/payout.conf (PAYOUT_* overrides).\nset -u\nexport LC_ALL=C.UTF-8\nPAYOUT_HOME=$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\nexport PAYOUT_HOME\n. \"$PAYOUT_HOME/steps/_env.sh\"\n\nusage() { sed -n '3,9p' \"$0\" | sed 's/^# \\{0,1\\}//'; }\n\ncmd_run() {\n  local date=$1 step rc\n  for step in \"$PAYOUT_HOME\"/steps/[0-9][0-9]-*.sh; do\n    bash \"$step\" \"$date\"\n    rc=$?\n    if [ \"$rc\" -ne 0 ]; then\n      warn \"step $(basename \"$step\") failed (exit $rc)\"\n      return \"$rc\"\n    fi\n  done\n  log \"run $date complete\"\n}\n\ncmd_manifest() {\n  local date=$1 p name ticket rows\n  printf '# %s\\n' \"$(date_dash \"$date\")\"\n  manifest_show \"$date\" | while IFS='|' read -r _ p name ticket rows; do\n    printf '%-5s %-40s %s %4s\\n' \"$p\" \"$name\" \"$ticket\" \"$rows\"\n  done\n}\n\n[ $# -ge 1 ] || { usage; exit 64; }\ncmd=$1; shift\ncase \"$cmd\" in\n  run)      [ $# -eq 1 ] || { usage; exit 64; }; cmd_run \"$(check_date \"$1\")\" ;;\n  manifest) [ $# -eq 1 ] || { usage; exit 64; }; cmd_manifest \"$(check_date \"$1\")\" ;;\n  receipts) [ $# -eq 3 ] || { usage; exit 64; }\n            receipts_report \"$1\" \"$(check_date \"$2\")\" \"$(check_date \"$3\")\" ;;\n  partners) active_partners ;;\n  -h|--help|help) usage ;;\n  *) usage; exit 64 ;;\nesac\n----\n=== lib/chunk.sh\n# chunk.sh — splits a row file into parts of at most N rows.\n\n# chunk_rows FILE MAX PREFIX — writes PREFIX.01, PREFIX.02, ... and prints the\n# number of parts. An empty FILE still yields one (empty) part so the partner\n# receives a file for every settlement day.\nchunk_rows() {\n  local file=$1 max=$2 prefix=$3 rows parts\n  rows=$(wc -l < \"$file\" | tr -d ' ')\n  if [ \"$rows\" -le \"$max\" ]; then\n    cp -f \"$file\" \"$prefix.01\" || return 1\n    printf '1'\n    return 0\n  fi\n  split -l \"$max\" -d -a 2 --numeric-suffixes=1 \"$file\" \"$prefix.\" || return 1\n  parts=$(( (rows + max - 1) / max ))\n  printf '%d' \"$parts\"\n}\n=== lib/common.sh\n# common.sh — logging, configuration loading and small guards shared by\n# the wrapper and every step script.\n\nlog()  { printf '[%s] %s\\n' \"${PAYOUT_STEP:-payout}\" \"$*\" >&2; }\nwarn() { printf '[%s] warn: %s\\n' \"${PAYOUT_STEP:-payout}\" \"$*\" >&2; }\ndie()  { printf '[%s] error: %s\\n' \"${PAYOUT_STEP:-payout}\" \"$*\" >&2; exit \"${2:-1}\"; }\n\nload_conf() {\n  local f=\"$PAYOUT_HOME/conf/payout.conf\"\n  [ -r \"$f\" ] || die \"missing config $f\"\n  # shellcheck disable=SC1090\n  . \"$f\"\n}\n\nrequire_file() {\n  [ -f \"$1\" ] || die \"${2:-file} not found: $1\"\n  [ -r \"$1\" ] || die \"${2:-file} not readable: $1\"\n}\n\nensure_dir() {\n  mkdir -p \"$1\" 2>/dev/null || die \"cannot create directory $1\"\n  [ -w \"$1\" ] || die \"directory not writable: $1\"\n}\n\n# Validates a business date in YYYYMMDD form and echoes it back.\ncheck_date() {\n  local d=$1\n  case \"$d\" in\n    [0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]) ;;\n    *) die \"bad date '$d' (want YYYYMMDD)\" ;;\n  esac\n  local m=$((10#${d:4:2})) day=$((10#${d:6:2}))\n  [ \"$m\" -ge 1 ] && [ \"$m\" -le 12 ] || die \"bad month in $d\"\n  [ \"$day\" -ge 1 ] && [ \"$day\" -le 31 ] || die \"bad day in $d\"\n  printf '%s' \"$d\"\n}\n\n# Per-run working area: $WORK_DIR/<date>\nrun_dir() { printf '%s/%s' \"$WORK_DIR\" \"$1\"; }\n\n# Active partner codes, one per line.\nactive_partners() {\n  require_file \"$PARTNERS_FILE\" \"partner list\"\n  awk -F'|' '!/^#/ && NF >= 4 && $4 == \"A\" { print $1 }' \"$PARTNERS_FILE\"\n}\n=== lib/csvfile.sh\n# csvfile.sh — settlement file body (PAY-IF-03 rev.2).\n#\n#   H,<sender>,<partner>,<date>,<part>/<parts>\n#   D,<txn>,<date>,<amount>,<fee>,<net>      one per transaction\n#   T,<detail count>,<net total>\n#\n# Lines end in CRLF when LINE_END=crlf.\n\n_eol() { [ \"${LINE_END:-lf}\" = crlf ] && printf '\\r\\n' || printf '\\n'; }\n\n# csv_render DATE PARTNER PART PARTS < rows(txn<TAB>amount<TAB>fee)\ncsv_render() {\n  local date=$1 partner=$2 part=$3 parts=$4 txn amount fee net n=0 total=0\n  printf 'H,%s,%s,%s,%d/%d' \"$SENDER_ID\" \"$partner\" \"$date\" \"$part\" \"$parts\"; _eol\n  while IFS=$'\\t' read -r txn amount fee; do\n    [ -n \"$txn\" ] || continue\n    net=$(money_net \"$amount\" \"$fee\")\n    printf 'D,%s,%s,%s,%s,%s' \"$txn\" \"$date\" \"$amount\" \"$fee\" \"$net\"; _eol\n    n=$((n + 1)); total=$((total + net))\n  done\n  printf 'T,%d,%d' \"$n\" \"$total\"; _eol\n}\n=== lib/dates.sh\n# dates.sh — business date helpers (GNU date).\n\n# \"20261005\" -> \"2026-10-05\"\ndate_dash() { printf '%s-%s-%s' \"${1:0:4}\" \"${1:4:2}\" \"${1:6:2}\"; }\n\n# \"2026-10-05\" or \"20261005\" -> \"20261005\"\ndate_compact() { local d=${1//-/}; printf '%s' \"$d\"; }\n\n# date_next YYYYMMDD -> the following calendar day\ndate_next() { date -u -d \"$(date_dash \"$1\") +1 day\" +%Y%m%d; }\n\n# date_range FROM TO — every calendar day from FROM to TO inclusive.\n# Partners settle seven days a week, so weekends are included.\ndate_range() {\n  local d=$1 end=$2 guard=0\n  while [ \"$d\" -le \"$end\" ]; do\n    printf '%s\\n' \"$d\"\n    d=$(date_next \"$d\")\n    guard=$((guard + 1))\n    [ \"$guard\" -le 400 ] || { warn \"date range too long: $1..$2\"; return 1; }\n  done\n}\n=== lib/manifest.sh\n# manifest.sh — local record of what was handed to the transfer CLI.\n# One line per file: date|partner|name|ticket|rows\n\nmanifest_file() { printf '%s/manifest.psv' \"$OUT_DIR\"; }\n\nmanifest_add() {\n  ensure_dir \"$OUT_DIR\"\n  printf '%s|%s|%s|%s|%s\\n' \"$1\" \"$2\" \"$3\" \"$4\" \"$5\" >> \"$(manifest_file)\"\n}\n\n# A re-run of the same day appends new lines; keep only the latest line for\n# each (date, partner, name).\nmanifest_compact() {\n  local f tmp\n  f=$(manifest_file)\n  [ -f \"$f\" ] || return 0\n  tmp=\"$f.tmp\"\n  awk -F'|' '{ k = $1 \"|\" $2 \"|\" $3; if (!(k in last)) order[++n] = k; last[k] = $0 }\n             END { for (i = 1; i <= n; i++) print last[order[i]] }' \"$f\" > \"$tmp\" \\\n    && mv -f \"$tmp\" \"$f\"\n}\n\n# manifest_show DATE — the day's lines, partner order.\nmanifest_show() {\n  local f\n  f=$(manifest_file)\n  [ -f \"$f\" ] || return 0\n  awk -F'|' -v d=\"$1\" '$1 == d' \"$f\" | sort -t'|' -k2,2 -k3,3\n}\n=== lib/money.sh\n# money.sh — integer KRW arithmetic and formatting.\n\n# money_net AMOUNT FEE -> amount minus fee\nmoney_net() { printf '%d' $(( 10#$1 - 10#$2 )); }\n\n# money_fmt N -> \"1,234,567\"\nmoney_fmt() {\n  local n=$1 sign=\"\" out=\"\"\n  case \"$n\" in -*) sign=\"-\"; n=${n#-} ;; esac\n  while [ ${#n} -gt 3 ]; do\n    out=\",${n: -3}$out\"\n    n=${n:0:${#n}-3}\n  done\n  printf '%s%s%s' \"$sign\" \"$n\" \"$out\"\n}\n=== lib/naming.sh\n# naming.sh — remote file names for settlement files.\n#\n#   HBP_SETTLE_<partner>_<YYYYMMDD>.csv          one file for the day\n#   HBP_SETTLE_<partner>_<YYYYMMDD>_<n>.csv      day split into several parts\n\n# settle_name PARTNER DATE PART PARTS\nsettle_name() {\n  local partner=$1 date=$2 part=$3 parts=$4\n  local base=\"${FILE_PREFIX}_${partner}_${date}\"\n  if [ \"$parts\" -gt 1 ]; then\n    base=\"${base}_${part}\"\n  fi\n  printf '%s.%s' \"$base\" \"$FILE_EXT\"\n}\n=== lib/receipts.sh\n# receipts.sh — what the partner can actually download, per settlement day.\n# Reads the partner's box through the transfer CLI and totals the detail rows.\n\n# receipts_rows PARTNER — date<TAB>net for every detail row in the partner's box.\nreceipts_rows() {\n  local partner=$1 name bytes ticket\n  xfer_ls \"$partner\" | while IFS=$'\\t' read -r name bytes ticket; do\n    [ -n \"$name\" ] || continue\n    xfer_pull \"$partner\" \"$name\" | tr -d '\\r' | awk -F, '$1 == \"D\" { print $3 \"\\t\" $6 }'\n  done\n}\n\n# receipts_report PARTNER FROM TO\nreceipts_report() {\n  local partner=$1 from=$2 to=$3 rows d cnt net\n  rows=$(receipts_rows \"$partner\")\n  printf '# partner %s  %s..%s\\n' \"$partner\" \"$(date_dash \"$from\")\" \"$(date_dash \"$to\")\"\n  for d in $(date_range \"$from\" \"$to\"); do\n    cnt=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$rows\" | awk -F'\\t' -v d=\"$d\" '$1 == d { n++ } END { print n + 0 }')\n    net=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$rows\" | awk -F'\\t' -v d=\"$d\" '$1 == d { s += $2 } END { print s + 0 }')\n    if [ \"$cnt\" -eq 0 ]; then\n      printf '%s  %4s  %15s\\n' \"$(date_dash \"$d\")\" \"-\" \"-\"\n    else\n      printf '%s  %4d  %15s\\n' \"$(date_dash \"$d\")\" \"$cnt\" \"$(money_fmt \"$net\")\"\n    fi\n  done\n}\n=== lib/txns.sh\n# txns.sh — reads the acquiring extract (settle_date, partner, txn, amount, fee).\n\n# txns_for DATE PARTNER — that partner's rows for DATE, ordered by txn id.\ntxns_for() {\n  require_file \"$TXN_FILE\" \"transaction extract\"\n  awk -F'\\t' -v d=\"$1\" -v p=\"$2\" '\n    /^#/ || NF < 5 { next }\n    $1 == d && $2 == p { print $3 \"\\t\" $4 \"\\t\" $5 }\n  ' \"$TXN_FILE\" | sort -t$'\\t' -k1,1\n}\n\n# txns_count DATE PARTNER\ntxns_count() { txns_for \"$1\" \"$2\" | wc -l | tr -d ' '; }\n=== lib/xfer.sh\n# xfer.sh — thin wrapper around the transfer vendor CLI.\n\n_xferq() { \"$XFERQ\" \"$@\"; }\n\n# xfer_send PARTNER FILE NAME — uploads FILE as NAME and prints the ticket.\n# Transient spool errors are retried; a malformed answer counts as a failure.\nxfer_send() {\n  local partner=$1 file=$2 name=$3 out rc try=0\n  while :; do\n    out=$(_xferq send --to \"$partner\" --file \"$file\" --as \"$name\" 2>&1); rc=$?\n    if [ \"$rc\" -eq 0 ]; then\n      case \"$out\" in\n        T[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]) printf '%s' \"$out\"; return 0 ;;\n        *) warn \"unexpected answer from transfer CLI: $out\"; return 1 ;;\n      esac\n    fi\n    try=$((try + 1))\n    if [ \"$try\" -gt \"$SEND_RETRIES\" ]; then\n      warn \"send $name to $partner failed ($out, exit $rc)\"\n      return 1\n    fi\n    log \"retrying $name ($out)\"\n  done\n}\n\n# xfer_ls PARTNER — name<TAB>bytes<TAB>ticket for files in the partner's box.\nxfer_ls() { _xferq ls --to \"$1\"; }\n\n# xfer_pull PARTNER NAME — file contents on stdout.\nxfer_pull() { _xferq pull --to \"$1\" --name \"$2\"; }\n=== steps/10-extract.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Step 10 — cut the day's rows per active partner out of the acquiring extract.\nPAYOUT_STEP=extract\n. \"$(dirname \"$0\")/_env.sh\"\n\ndate=$(check_date \"${1:-}\")\ndir=$(run_dir \"$date\")\nrm -rf \"$dir\"\nensure_dir \"$dir/rows\"\n\ntotal=0\nfor p in $(active_partners); do\n  txns_for \"$date\" \"$p\" > \"$dir/rows/$p.tsv\" || die \"extract failed for $p\"\n  n=$(wc -l < \"$dir/rows/$p.tsv\" | tr -d ' ')\n  total=$((total + n))\n  log \"$p: $n rows\"\ndone\nlog \"extracted $total rows for $date\"\n=== steps/20-build.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Step 20 — build the settlement files (split to the partner row limit).\nPAYOUT_STEP=build\n. \"$(dirname \"$0\")/_env.sh\"\n\ndate=$(check_date \"${1:-}\")\ndir=$(run_dir \"$date\")\n[ -d \"$dir/rows\" ] || die \"nothing extracted for $date\"\nensure_dir \"$dir/files\"\n: > \"$dir/files.lst\"\n\nfor rows in \"$dir\"/rows/*.tsv; do\n  [ -e \"$rows\" ] || continue\n  p=$(basename \"$rows\" .tsv)\n  parts=$(chunk_rows \"$rows\" \"$MAX_ROWS_PER_FILE\" \"$dir/rows/$p.part\") || die \"split failed for $p\"\n  for i in $(seq 1 \"$parts\"); do\n    chunk=$(printf '%s/rows/%s.part.%02d' \"$dir\" \"$p\" \"$i\")\n    name=$(settle_name \"$p\" \"$date\" \"$i\" \"$parts\")\n    csv_render \"$date\" \"$p\" \"$i\" \"$parts\" < \"$chunk\" > \"$dir/files/$name\" \\\n      || die \"render failed for $name\"\n    printf '%s|%s|%s\\n' \"$p\" \"$name\" \"$(wc -l < \"$chunk\" | tr -d ' ')\" >> \"$dir/files.lst\"\n  done\ndone\nlog \"built $(wc -l < \"$dir/files.lst\" | tr -d ' ') files\"\n=== steps/30-ship.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Step 30 — hand every built file to the transfer CLI and record the ticket.\nPAYOUT_STEP=ship\n. \"$(dirname \"$0\")/_env.sh\"\n\ndate=$(check_date \"${1:-}\")\ndir=$(run_dir \"$date\")\nrequire_file \"$dir/files.lst\" \"file list\"\n\nsent=0 failed=0\nwhile IFS='|' read -r p name rows; do\n  [ -n \"$name\" ] || continue\n  if ticket=$(xfer_send \"$p\" \"$dir/files/$name\" \"$name\"); then\n    manifest_add \"$date\" \"$p\" \"$name\" \"$ticket\" \"$rows\"\n    log \"sent $name ($rows rows) -> $ticket\"\n    sent=$((sent + 1))\n  else\n    failed=$((failed + 1))\n  fi\ndone < \"$dir/files.lst\"\nmanifest_compact\n[ \"$failed\" -eq 0 ] || die \"$failed file(s) not sent\" 3\nlog \"shipped $sent files for $date\"\n=== steps/_env.sh\n# Sourced by every step script. Expects PAYOUT_HOME (set by bin/payout).\n: \"${PAYOUT_HOME:?run steps through bin/payout}\"\nfor _lib in common dates money txns csvfile chunk naming xfer manifest receipts; do\n  # shellcheck disable=SC1090\n  . \"$PAYOUT_HOME/lib/$_lib.sh\"\ndone\nunset _lib\nload_conf\n=== conf/partners.conf\n# code|name|cycle|status   (status I = suspended, no files are produced)\nP001|한빛마트|daily|A\nP002|온누리약국체인|daily|A\nP003|바다횟집 연합|daily|A\nP004|구)스마일편의점|daily|I\n=== conf/payout.conf\n# payout.conf — defaults for the merchant payout file batch.\n# Every value can be overridden from the environment (PAYOUT_*); the scheduler\n# and the tests use that to point the batch at other directories.\n\nTXN_FILE=${PAYOUT_TXN_FILE:-$PAYOUT_HOME/fixtures/txns-202610.tsv}\nPARTNERS_FILE=${PAYOUT_PARTNERS_FILE:-$PAYOUT_HOME/conf/partners.conf}\nWORK_DIR=${PAYOUT_WORK_DIR:-/var/tmp/payout}\nOUT_DIR=${PAYOUT_OUT_DIR:-/var/lib/payout}\n\n# Transfer CLI (vendor). Its spool directory comes from XFERQ_HOME.\nXFERQ=${PAYOUT_XFERQ:-$PAYOUT_HOME/vendor/bin/xferq}\nSEND_RETRIES=${PAYOUT_SEND_RETRIES:-2}\n\n# Settlement file layout agreed with the partners (PAY-IF-03 rev.2)\nFILE_PREFIX=HBP_SETTLE\nFILE_EXT=csv\nSENDER_ID=HBP\n# Partners load at most this many detail rows per file.\nMAX_ROWS_PER_FILE=20\n# Partner intake runs on Windows hosts.\nLINE_END=crlf","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d68e6247-81e1-42cc-8b61-dd761841c049","uuid":"8d94d86a-4236-4891-bb8c-93ecfae6c851","timestamp":"2026-10-09T04:27:50.235Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# payout — 가맹 파트너 일일 정산 파일 배치\n\n카드 매입 추출(`txns-YYYYMM.tsv`)에서 파트너별·일자별 정산 내역을 잘라 정산 파일(PAY-IF-03 rev.2)을 만들고,\n파일 전송 벤더 CLI(`vendor/bin/xferq`, 벤더가 바이너리로 제공)로 파트너 수신함에 올린다.\n\n## 실행\n\n```\nbin/payout run 20261005                    # extract → build → ship\nbin/payout manifest 20261005               # 그날 전송 CLI에 넘긴 파일과 접수 번호\nbin/payout receipts P001 20261001 20261007 # 파트너가 실제로 내려받을 수 있는 일자별 건수·금액\nbin/payout partners                        # 활성 파트너\n```\n\n스케줄러는 매일 07:00에 전날 일자로 `bin/payout run`을 돌리고, exit 0이 아니면 당직에게 알린다.\n`XFERQ_HOME`(전송 CLI 스풀 디렉터리)은 스케줄러 환경에서 지정한다. 벤더 사용법은 `vendor/bin/xferq --help`.\n\n## 구성\n\n| 경로 | 내용 |\n|------|------|\n| `bin/payout` | 진입점. 서브커맨드 분기, 단계 순차 실행 |\n| `steps/NN-*.sh` | 단계 스크립트(번호 순). 각자 `_env.sh`로 lib·설정을 읽는다 |\n| `lib/` | 공용 함수 (추출, 분할, 파일 본문, 파일 이름, 전송, 매니페스트, 수신 확인 등) |\n| `conf/payout.conf` | 디렉터리·파일 규격 설정. `PAYOUT_*` 환경변수로 덮어쓴다 |\n| `conf/partners.conf` | 파트너 목록(상태 I는 정지 — 파일을 만들지 않음) |\n| `fixtures/` | 샘플 매입 추출(운영 데이터에서 금액·번호를 바꾼 것) |\n| `tests/` | `bash tests/run.sh` — 단위 테스트 + 샘플 주간 E2E |\n\n## 정산 파일 규격 메모 (PAY-IF-03 rev.2)\n\n- 파일명: `HBP_SETTLE_<파트너코드>_<YYYYMMDD>.csv` — 파트너와 합의한 접두. 파트너 쪽 적재기는 이 접두로 파일을 고른다.\n- 파트너 적재기는 파일당 명세(D) 최대 20행까지만 받는다. 넘는 날은 여러 파일로 나눠 보낸다(헤더의 `n/총수`).\n- 본문: `H`(헤더) / `D`(명세, 거래당 1행) / `T`(트레일러 — 명세 건수·순액 합계). 줄 끝은 CRLF.\n- 정산은 주말 포함 매일 나간다. 거래가 없는 날도 빈 파일(H·T만)을 보낸다.\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Runs the full test suite.\nexec bash \"$(dirname \"$0\")/tests/run.sh\"\n----\nbin:\npayout\n\nconf:\npartners.conf\npayout.conf\n\nfixtures:\ntxns-202610.tsv\n\nlib:\nchunk.sh\ncommon.sh\ncsvfile.sh\ndates.sh\nmanifest.sh\nmoney.sh\nnaming.sh\nreceipts.sh\ntxns.sh\nxfer.sh\n\nsteps:\n10-extract.sh\n20-build.sh\n30-ship.sh\n_env.sh\n\ntests:\nlib.sh\nrun.sh\ntest_chunk.sh\ntest_csvfile.sh\ntest_dates.sh\ntest_partner_delivery.sh\n\nvendor:\nbin\n\nvendor/bin:\nxferq\n----\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# payout — merchant settlement files for card-acquiring partners.\n#\n#   payout run DATE                  extract → build → ship\n#   payout manifest DATE             files handed to the transfer CLI that day\n#   payout receipts PARTNER FROM TO  what the partner can download, per day\n#   payout partners                  active partner codes\n#\n# DATE is YYYYMMDD. Configuration: conf/payout.conf (PAYOUT_* overrides).\nset -u\nexport LC_ALL=C.UTF-8\nPAYOUT_HOME=$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\nexport PAYOUT_HOME\n. \"$PAYOUT_HOME/steps/_env.sh\"\n\nusage() { sed -n '3,9p' \"$0\" | sed 's/^# \\{0,1\\}//'; }\n\ncmd_run() {\n  local date=$1 step rc\n  for step in \"$PAYOUT_HOME\"/steps/[0-9][0-9]-*.sh; do\n    bash \"$step\" \"$date\"\n    rc=$?\n    if [ \"$rc\" -ne 0 ]; then\n      warn \"step $(basename \"$step\") failed (exit $rc)\"\n      return \"$rc\"\n    fi\n  done\n  log \"run $date complete\"\n}\n\ncmd_manifest() {\n  local date=$1 p name ticket rows\n  printf '# %s\\n' \"$(date_dash \"$date\")\"\n  manifest_show \"$date\" | while IFS='|' read -r _ p name ticket rows; do\n    printf '%-5s %-40s %s %4s\\n' \"$p\" \"$name\" \"$ticket\" \"$rows\"\n  done\n}\n\n[ $# -ge 1 ] || { usage; exit 64; }\ncmd=$1; shift\ncase \"$cmd\" in\n  run)      [ $# -eq 1 ] || { usage; exit 64; }; cmd_run \"$(check_date \"$1\")\" ;;\n  manifest) [ $# -eq 1 ] || { usage; exit 64; }; cmd_manifest \"$(check_date \"$1\")\" ;;\n  receipts) [ $# -eq 3 ] || { usage; exit 64; }\n            receipts_report \"$1\" \"$(check_date \"$2\")\" \"$(check_date \"$3\")\" ;;\n  partners) active_partners ;;\n  -h|--help|help) usage ;;\n  *) usage; exit 64 ;;\nesac\n----\n=== lib/chunk.sh\n# chunk.sh — splits a row file into parts of at most N rows.\n\n# chunk_rows FILE MAX PREFIX — writes PREFIX.01, PREFIX.02, ... and prints the\n# number of parts. An empty FILE still yields one (empty) part so the partner\n# receives a file for every settlement day.\nchunk_rows() {\n  local file=$1 max=$2 prefix=$3 rows parts\n  rows=$(wc -l < \"$file\" | tr -d ' ')\n  if [ \"$rows\" -le \"$max\" ]; then\n    cp -f \"$file\" \"$prefix.01\" || return 1\n    printf '1'\n    return 0\n  fi\n  split -l \"$max\" -d -a 2 --numeric-suffixes=1 \"$file\" \"$prefix.\" || return 1\n  parts=$(( (rows + max - 1) / max ))\n  printf '%d' \"$parts\"\n}\n=== lib/common.sh\n# common.sh — logging, configuration loading and small guards shared by\n# the wrapper and every step script.\n\nlog()  { printf '[%s] %s\\n' \"${PAYOUT_STEP:-payout}\" \"$*\" >&2; }\nwarn() { printf '[%s] warn: %s\\n' \"${PAYOUT_STEP:-payout}\" \"$*\" >&2; }\ndie()  { printf '[%s] error: %s\\n' \"${PAYOUT_STEP:-payout}\" \"$*\" >&2; exit \"${2:-1}\"; }\n\nload_conf() {\n  local f=\"$PAYOUT_HOME/conf/payout.conf\"\n  [ -r \"$f\" ] || die \"missing config $f\"\n  # shellcheck disable=SC1090\n  . \"$f\"\n}\n\nrequire_file() {\n  [ -f \"$1\" ] || die \"${2:-file} not found: $1\"\n  [ -r \"$1\" ] || die \"${2:-file} not readable: $1\"\n}\n\nensure_dir() {\n  mkdir -p \"$1\" 2>/dev/null || die \"cannot create directory $1\"\n  [ -w \"$1\" ] || die \"directory not writable: $1\"\n}\n\n# Validates a business date in YYYYMMDD form and echoes it back.\ncheck_date() {\n  local d=$1\n  case \"$d\" in\n    [0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]) ;;\n    *) die \"bad date '$d' (want YYYYMMDD)\" ;;\n  esac\n  local m=$((10#${d:4:2})) day=$((10#${d:6:2}))\n  [ \"$m\" -ge 1 ] && [ \"$m\" -le 12 ] || die \"bad month in $d\"\n  [ \"$day\" -ge 1 ] && [ \"$day\" -le 31 ] || die \"bad day in $d\"\n  printf '%s' \"$d\"\n}\n\n# Per-run working area: $WORK_DIR/<date>\nrun_dir() { printf '%s/%s' \"$WORK_DIR\" \"$1\"; }\n\n# Active partner codes, one per line.\nactive_partners() {\n  require_file \"$PARTNERS_FILE\" \"partner list\"\n  awk -F'|' '!/^#/ && NF >= 4 && $4 == \"A\" { print $1 }' \"$PARTNERS_FILE\"\n}\n=== lib/csvfile.sh\n# csvfile.sh — settlement file body (PAY-IF-03 rev.2).\n#\n#   H,<sender>,<partner>,<date>,<part>/<parts>\n#   D,<txn>,<date>,<amount>,<fee>,<net>      one per transaction\n#   T,<detail count>,<net total>\n#\n# Lines end in CRLF when LINE_END=crlf.\n\n_eol() { [ \"${LINE_END:-lf}\" = crlf ] && printf '\\r\\n' || printf '\\n'; }\n\n# csv_render DATE PARTNER PART PARTS < rows(txn<TAB>amount<TAB>fee)\ncsv_render() {\n  local date=$1 partner=$2 part=$3 parts=$4 txn amount fee net n=0 total=0\n  printf 'H,%s,%s,%s,%d/%d' \"$SENDER_ID\" \"$partner\" \"$date\" \"$part\" \"$parts\"; _eol\n  while IFS=$'\\t' read -r txn amount fee; do\n    [ -n \"$txn\" ] || continue\n    net=$(money_net \"$amount\" \"$fee\")\n    printf 'D,%s,%s,%s,%s,%s' \"$txn\" \"$date\" \"$amount\" \"$fee\" \"$net\"; _eol\n    n=$((n + 1)); total=$((total + net))\n  done\n  printf 'T,%d,%d' \"$n\" \"$total\"; _eol\n}\n=== lib/dates.sh\n# dates.sh — business date helpers (GNU date).\n\n# \"20261005\" -> \"2026-10-05\"\ndate_dash() { printf '%s-%s-%s' \"${1:0:4}\" \"${1:4:2}\" \"${1:6:2}\"; }\n\n# \"2026-10-05\" or \"20261005\" -> \"20261005\"\ndate_compact() { local d=${1//-/}; printf '%s' \"$d\"; }\n\n# date_next YYYYMMDD -> the following calendar day\ndate_next() { date -u -d \"$(date_dash \"$1\") +1 day\" +%Y%m%d; }\n\n# date_range FROM TO — every calendar day from FROM to TO inclusive.\n# Partners settle seven days a week, so weekends are included.\ndate_range() {\n  local d=$1 end=$2 guard=0\n  while [ \"$d\" -le \"$end\" ]; do\n    printf '%s\\n' \"$d\"\n    d=$(date_next \"$d\")\n    guard=$((guard + 1))\n    [ \"$guard\" -le 400 ] || { warn \"date range too long: $1..$2\"; return 1; }\n  done\n}\n=== lib/manifest.sh\n# manifest.sh — local record of what was handed to the transfer CLI.\n# One line per file: date|partner|name|ticket|rows\n\nmanifest_file() { printf '%s/manifest.psv' \"$OUT_DIR\"; }\n\nmanifest_add() {\n  ensure_dir \"$OUT_DIR\"\n  printf '%s|%s|%s|%s|%s\\n' \"$1\" \"$2\" \"$3\" \"$4\" \"$5\" >> \"$(manifest_file)\"\n}\n\n# A re-run of the same day appends new lines; keep only the latest line for\n# each (date, partner, name).\nmanifest_compact() {\n  local f tmp\n  f=$(manifest_file)\n  [ -f \"$f\" ] || return 0\n  tmp=\"$f.tmp\"\n  awk -F'|' '{ k = $1 \"|\" $2 \"|\" $3; if (!(k in last)) order[++n] = k; last[k] = $0 }\n             END { for (i = 1; i <= n; i++) print last[order[i]] }' \"$f\" > \"$tmp\" \\\n    && mv -f \"$tmp\" \"$f\"\n}\n\n# manifest_show DATE — the day's lines, partner order.\nmanifest_show() {\n  local f\n  f=$(manifest_file)\n  [ -f \"$f\" ] || return 0\n  awk -F'|' -v d=\"$1\" '$1 == d' \"$f\" | sort -t'|' -k2,2 -k3,3\n}\n=== lib/money.sh\n# money.sh — integer KRW arithmetic and formatting.\n\n# money_net AMOUNT FEE -> amount minus fee\nmoney_net() { printf '%d' $(( 10#$1 - 10#$2 )); }\n\n# money_fmt N -> \"1,234,567\"\nmoney_fmt() {\n  local n=$1 sign=\"\" out=\"\"\n  case \"$n\" in -*) sign=\"-\"; n=${n#-} ;; esac\n  while [ ${#n} -gt 3 ]; do\n    out=\",${n: -3}$out\"\n    n=${n:0:${#n}-3}\n  done\n  printf '%s%s%s' \"$sign\" \"$n\" \"$out\"\n}\n=== lib/naming.sh\n# naming.sh — remote file names for settlement files.\n#\n#   HBP_SETTLE_<partner>_<YYYYMMDD>.csv          one file for the day\n#   HBP_SETTLE_<partner>_<YYYYMMDD>_<n>.csv      day split into several parts\n\n# settle_name PARTNER DATE PART PARTS\nsettle_name() {\n  local partner=$1 date=$2 part=$3 parts=$4\n  local base=\"${FILE_PREFIX}_${partner}_${date}\"\n  if [ \"$parts\" -gt 1 ]; then\n    base=\"${base}_${part}\"\n  fi\n  printf '%s.%s' \"$base\" \"$FILE_EXT\"\n}\n=== lib/receipts.sh\n# receipts.sh — what the partner can actually download, per settlement day.\n# Reads the partner's box through the transfer CLI and totals the detail rows.\n\n# receipts_rows PARTNER — date<TAB>net for every detail row in the partner's box.\nreceipts_rows() {\n  local partner=$1 name bytes ticket\n  xfer_ls \"$partner\" | while IFS=$'\\t' read -r name bytes ticket; do\n    [ -n \"$name\" ] || continue\n    xfer_pull \"$partner\" \"$name\" | tr -d '\\r' | awk -F, '$1 == \"D\" { print $3 \"\\t\" $6 }'\n  done\n}\n\n# receipts_report PARTNER FROM TO\nreceipts_report() {\n  local partner=$1 from=$2 to=$3 rows d cnt net\n  rows=$(receipts_rows \"$partner\")\n  printf '# partner %s  %s..%s\\n' \"$partner\" \"$(date_dash \"$from\")\" \"$(date_dash \"$to\")\"\n  for d in $(date_range \"$from\" \"$to\"); do\n    cnt=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$rows\" | awk -F'\\t' -v d=\"$d\" '$1 == d { n++ } END { print n + 0 }')\n    net=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$rows\" | awk -F'\\t' -v d=\"$d\" '$1 == d { s += $2 } END { print s + 0 }')\n    if [ \"$cnt\" -eq 0 ]; then\n      printf '%s  %4s  %15s\\n' \"$(date_dash \"$d\")\" \"-\" \"-\"\n    else\n      printf '%s  %4d  %15s\\n' \"$(date_dash \"$d\")\" \"$cnt\" \"$(money_fmt \"$net\")\"\n    fi\n  done\n}\n=== lib/txns.sh\n# txns.sh — reads the acquiring extract (settle_date, partner, txn, amount, fee).\n\n# txns_for DATE PARTNER — that partner's rows for DATE, ordered by txn id.\ntxns_for() {\n  require_file \"$TXN_FILE\" \"transaction extract\"\n  awk -F'\\t' -v d=\"$1\" -v p=\"$2\" '\n    /^#/ || NF < 5 { next }\n    $1 == d && $2 == p { print $3 \"\\t\" $4 \"\\t\" $5 }\n  ' \"$TXN_FILE\" | sort -t$'\\t' -k1,1\n}\n\n# txns_count DATE PARTNER\ntxns_count() { txns_for \"$1\" \"$2\" | wc -l | tr -d ' '; }\n=== lib/xfer.sh\n# xfer.sh — thin wrapper around the transfer vendor CLI.\n\n_xferq() { \"$XFERQ\" \"$@\"; }\n\n# xfer_send PARTNER FILE NAME — uploads FILE as NAME and prints the ticket.\n# Transient spool errors are retried; a malformed answer counts as a failure.\nxfer_send() {\n  local partner=$1 file=$2 name=$3 out rc try=0\n  while :; do\n    out=$(_xferq send --to \"$partner\" --file \"$file\" --as \"$name\" 2>&1); rc=$?\n    if [ \"$rc\" -eq 0 ]; then\n      case \"$out\" in\n        T[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]) printf '%s' \"$out\"; return 0 ;;\n        *) warn \"unexpected answer from transfer CLI: $out\"; return 1 ;;\n      esac\n    fi\n    try=$((try + 1))\n    if [ \"$try\" -gt \"$SEND_RETRIES\" ]; then\n      warn \"send $name to $partner failed ($out, exit $rc)\"\n      return 1\n    fi\n    log \"retrying $name ($out)\"\n  done\n}\n\n# xfer_ls PARTNER — name<TAB>bytes<TAB>ticket for files in the partner's box.\nxfer_ls() { _xferq ls --to \"$1\"; }\n\n# xfer_pull PARTNER NAME — file contents on stdout.\nxfer_pull() { _xferq pull --to \"$1\" --name \"$2\"; }\n=== steps/10-extract.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Step 10 — cut the day's rows per active partner out of the acquiring extract.\nPAYOUT_STEP=extract\n. \"$(dirname \"$0\")/_env.sh\"\n\ndate=$(check_date \"${1:-}\")\ndir=$(run_dir \"$date\")\nrm -rf \"$dir\"\nensure_dir \"$dir/rows\"\n\ntotal=0\nfor p in $(active_partners); do\n  txns_for \"$date\" \"$p\" > \"$dir/rows/$p.tsv\" || die \"extract failed for $p\"\n  n=$(wc -l < \"$dir/rows/$p.tsv\" | tr -d ' ')\n  total=$((total + n))\n  log \"$p: $n rows\"\ndone\nlog \"extracted $total rows for $date\"\n=== steps/20-build.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Step 20 — build the settlement files (split to the partner row limit).\nPAYOUT_STEP=build\n. \"$(dirname \"$0\")/_env.sh\"\n\ndate=$(check_date \"${1:-}\")\ndir=$(run_dir \"$date\")\n[ -d \"$dir/rows\" ] || die \"nothing extracted for $date\"\nensure_dir \"$dir/files\"\n: > \"$dir/files.lst\"\n\nfor rows in \"$dir\"/rows/*.tsv; do\n  [ -e \"$rows\" ] || continue\n  p=$(basename \"$rows\" .tsv)\n  parts=$(chunk_rows \"$rows\" \"$MAX_ROWS_PER_FILE\" \"$dir/rows/$p.part\") || die \"split failed for $p\"\n  for i in $(seq 1 \"$parts\"); do\n    chunk=$(printf '%s/rows/%s.part.%02d' \"$dir\" \"$p\" \"$i\")\n    name=$(settle_name \"$p\" \"$date\" \"$i\" \"$parts\")\n    csv_render \"$date\" \"$p\" \"$i\" \"$parts\" < \"$chunk\" > \"$dir/files/$name\" \\\n      || die \"render failed for $name\"\n    printf '%s|%s|%s\\n' \"$p\" \"$name\" \"$(wc -l < \"$chunk\" | tr -d ' ')\" >> \"$dir/files.lst\"\n  done\ndone\nlog \"built $(wc -l < \"$dir/files.lst\" | tr -d ' ') files\"\n=== steps/30-ship.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Step 30 — hand every built file to the transfer CLI and record the ticket.\nPAYOUT_STEP=ship\n. \"$(dirname \"$0\")/_env.sh\"\n\ndate=$(check_date \"${1:-}\")\ndir=$(run_dir \"$date\")\nrequire_file \"$dir/files.lst\" \"file list\"\n\nsent=0 failed=0\nwhile IFS='|' read -r p name rows; do\n  [ -n \"$name\" ] || continue\n  if ticket=$(xfer_send \"$p\" \"$dir/files/$name\" \"$name\"); then\n    manifest_add \"$date\" \"$p\" \"$name\" \"$ticket\" \"$rows\"\n    log \"sent $name ($rows rows) -> $ticket\"\n    sent=$((sent + 1))\n  else\n    failed=$((failed + 1))\n  fi\ndone < \"$dir/files.lst\"\nmanifest_compact\n[ \"$failed\" -eq 0 ] || die \"$failed file(s) not sent\" 3\nlog \"shipped $sent files for $date\"\n=== steps/_env.sh\n# Sourced by every step script. Expects PAYOUT_HOME (set by bin/payout).\n: \"${PAYOUT_HOME:?run steps through bin/payout}\"\nfor _lib in common dates money txns csvfile chunk naming xfer manifest receipts; do\n  # shellcheck disable=SC1090\n  . \"$PAYOUT_HOME/lib/$_lib.sh\"\ndone\nunset _lib\nload_conf\n=== conf/partners.conf\n# code|name|cycle|status   (status I = suspended, no files are produced)\nP001|한빛마트|daily|A\nP002|온누리약국체인|daily|A\nP003|바다횟집 연합|daily|A\nP004|구)스마일편의점|daily|I\n=== conf/payout.conf\n# payout.conf — defaults for the merchant payout file batch.\n# Every value can be overridden from the environment (PAYOUT_*); the scheduler\n# and the tests use that to point the batch at other directories.\n\nTXN_FILE=${PAYOUT_TXN_FILE:-$PAYOUT_HOME/fixtures/txns-202610.tsv}\nPARTNERS_FILE=${PAYOUT_PARTNERS_FILE:-$PAYOUT_HOME/conf/partners.conf}\nWORK_DIR=${PAYOUT_WORK_DIR:-/var/tmp/payout}\nOUT_DIR=${PAYOUT_OUT_DIR:-/var/lib/payout}\n\n# Transfer CLI (vendor). Its spool directory comes from XFERQ_HOME.\nXFERQ=${PAYOUT_XFERQ:-$PAYOUT_HOME/vendor/bin/xferq}\nSEND_RETRIES=${PAYOUT_SEND_RETRIES:-2}\n\n# Settlement file layout agreed with the partners (PAY-IF-03 rev.2)\nFILE_PREFIX=HBP_SETTLE\nFILE_EXT=csv\nSENDER_ID=HBP\n# Partners load at most this many detail rows per file.\nMAX_ROWS_PER_FILE=20\n# Partner intake runs on Windows hosts.\nLINE_END=crlf","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NiuGkYwbtNf5oo9pSwJPK5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
